  <data name="Guide_Tweak_Filters" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[h]Filters[/h] opens a filter window to hide items that match some criteria:</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Armoire_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Armoire</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Armoire_Intro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>GlamourLog adds two buttons next to the category arrows on the armoire window.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Armoire_StoreAll" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[h]Store all[/h] stores all eligible items from your inventory into the armoire. Ignores items in gearsets.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Dresser_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Dresser</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Dresser_Intro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>GlamourLog adds two buttons above the category arrows on the item deposit window.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Dresser_StoreAll" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[h]Store all[/h] stores all eligible items from your inventory into the dresser. Ignores items in gearsets.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_ChatAlerts_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Chat Alerts</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_ChatAlerts_Intro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When you loot an item that belongs to a glamour set, outfit progress is appended to the loot notice in chat.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_ChatAlerts_ExampleLoot" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>You obtain a {0}.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_ChatAlerts_AlreadyOwned" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If you already own the item in storage, the loot notice is left unchanged.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_LootWindow_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Loot Window</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_LootWindow_Intro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When the loot window is open, a badge is displayed on item icons for glam pieces you do not already own.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_LootWindow_Armoire" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[h]Armoire badge[/h] is shown on unowned armoire-eligible items.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_LootWindow_Dresser" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[h]Dresser badge[/h] is shown on unowned, non-armoire outfit pieces.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Counters_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Counters</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Counters_Completed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The bottom-right of the glamour log displays two numbers. The top number is the amount of sets you have completed out of the total number of sets available in the game.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Counters_Saved" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The bottom number is the amount of glamour dresser slots you have
saved by having these pieces stored as outfits instead of being loose inside the dresser.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Counters_FootnoteCombined" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Completed counter combines sets in the dresser and the armoire.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Counters_FootnoteMisc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>"Misc Armoire" are not included in either counters.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Icons_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Icons</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Icons_Checkmark" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[h]Checkmark[/h] is shown on a set icon when every piece is in your glamour dresser or armoire. Inventory does not count.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Icons_Unobtainable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[h]Unobtainable[/h] is shown on a set that cannot currently be obtained, e.g. a seasonal event set. These sets are excluded from the completion counters.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Icons_FadedDresser" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[h]Faded Dresser badge[/h] is shown on a complete set or owned piece when the item is in your dresser [e]not[/e] as part of a set.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Icons_Dresser" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[h]Dresser badge[/h] shown on a complete set or owned piece when the item is in your dresser as part of a set.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Icons_Armoire" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[h]Armoire badge[/h] is shown on a complete set or owned piece when the item is in your armoire.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Icons_WarningDresser" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[h]Dresser warning[/h] is shown if the item is currently stored in the dresser but could be stored in the armoire. Also applies to sets.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Integrations_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Plugin Integrations</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Integrations_Intro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>GlamourLog does not require other plugins to work, but it can be enhanced with other plugins.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Integrations_AllaganTools" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[e]Allagan Tools[/e] is used in the [h]currencies required[/h] section of [h]set details[/h] to get the amount of currency you have obtained in any inventory on your character. If not installed, this count will default to your standard inventory only.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Integrations_Vnavmesh" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[e]vnavmesh[/e] is used in the context menu of [h]Sources and Costs.[/h] If installed, this context menu entry will navigate you to the relevant source of the item.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_Integrations_AutoDuty" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[e]AutoDuty[/e] is used in the context menu of duty [h]Sources.[/h] If installed, this context menu entry will start an AutoDuty loop where your character will run the relevant dungeon until all missing outfit pieces are acquired.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_DataExport_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Data Export</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_DataExport_Intro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Here you can export your dresser and armoire data into a format importable into websites and other plugins.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_LogWindowSettings_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Glamour Log Window</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_LogWindowSettings_DisableClose" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Disable force window closing</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_LogWindowSettings_DisableClose_Tooltip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Prevents the game from closing the addon when you go through an area transition or cutscene. Will still hide the addon. Also disables the ability to close via ESC. Must be clicked manually.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_LogWindowSettings_PersistSearch" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Persist search</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Guide_LogWindowSettings_PersistSearch_Tooltip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Keeps the search text when the Glamour Log window is closed and reopened.</value>
  </data>
